        <mxCell id="oo83uOwNWfEE0Z5shK8--22" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;autosize=1;resizable=0;" value="Schema supported for SQL" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="170" x="150" y="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oo83uOwNWfEE0Z5shK8--63" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;autosize=1;resizable=0;" value="Need to have a blob storage interactive for how Aggregations and Python visualization files are built." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="560" x="-870" y="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oo83uOwNWfEE0Z5shK8--67" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Pipeline Steps&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. You log in as a user. This gives you a Login Credential used to access the application.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. You can upload or retrieve an existing dataset. If you are uploading a specific dataset, then it will create a new agent pipeline.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. As you run the statistics agent, the JSON will be uploaded to the statistics agent, then it will be passed down as data for the next step in the pipeline. For now if a session is blocked, then the dataset will not be saved and a new one will be uploaded.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. Insight agent will run, give a summary then it will go to the analysis agent for further investigation the input and response is saved ass JSON&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;5. Analysis agent will explain its thought process and what needs to be run.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;6. The Aggregation agent will build queries based on this. A visualization agent will take in this same information and run.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;7. The execution agent runs the files, and uploads the response. A Conversation agent will summarize the response and the findings to the user. Then this conversation agent may also help build the visualizations into a visualization field and take in additional prompts. It will decide if It wants to perform another analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="430" width="500" x="-640" y="550" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oo83uOwNWfEE0Z5shK8--68" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Blob Storage&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;Each session will have its own directory which stores the dataset and its parquet representation. Then a pipeline_id will be used to access that specific pipelines scripts and aggregations via python and parqueyt files.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;session/{session_id}/&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;original.csv&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;parquet.csv&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;pipelines/{pipeline_id}/&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;analysis.py&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;aggregations.parquet&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="270" x="-70" y="590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oo83uOwNWfEE0Z5shK8--69" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Agent Orchestration&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;Beta Ideas: We can use OpenAI Agents or something similar. similar to start_pipeline tool. (i.e a PipelineRunner class)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Conceptually an agent can have access to a PipelineService.create_pipeline() With openAI Agents SDK you can register the handler as a function tool.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;pre dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;class PipelineRunner:&lt;br&gt;    def __init__(self, repository, profiler, insight_agent,&lt;br&gt;                 analysis_agent, executor):&lt;br&gt;        self.repository = repository&lt;br&gt;        self.profiler = profiler&lt;br&gt;        self.insight_agent = insight_agent&lt;br&gt;        self.analysis_agent = analysis_agent&lt;br&gt;        self.executor = executor&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;    async def run(self, pipeline_id):&lt;br&gt;        pipeline = self.repository.load(pipeline_id)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;        # Each step loads its inputs and persists&lt;br&gt;        # its status, output references, and errors.&lt;br&gt;        await self.run_profile(pipeline)&lt;br&gt;        await self.run_insights(pipeline)&lt;br&gt;        await self.run_analysis(pipeline)&lt;br&gt;        await self.run_execution(pipeline)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="410" width="450" x="-1110" y="530" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oo83uOwNWfEE0Z5shK8--70" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Sprint 1 Goals:&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;Be able to import a dataset, go through the full 6 stage pipeline and have an output (simple) be recommended out to the user. There will be roles into building the frontend, and there will be roles for building stages of the pipeline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="330" x="-1530" y="540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oo83uOwNWfEE0Z5shK8--71" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Sprint 2 Goals:&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;Allow for a conversation agent to be embedded. The dataset information can be fetched by the conversation agent. A new dataset will be fetched from storage, it can be written to, editied, have additional information then be sent back to storage.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Download -&amp;gt; Edit Locally -&amp;gt; Upload Back.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="205" width="320" x="-1530" y="675" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nsMeJd_c_fcsu2wH51GI-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Endpoint Creation&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="290" x="-1650" y="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nsMeJd_c_fcsu2wH51GI-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Orchestrating Agent&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;A limit behind the multi-pipeline steps is how it can act as a limiting factor early on in interpretation. The outputs and analysis from the pipeline should be used an initial understanding and exploration that the orchestration model can use to continue investigating, verifying and extending the output.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Would Astra 6.1 possibly used as. a second analysis agent to the side of the existing pipeline to run aggregations? (Investigation agent which does an answer for specific questions, check disputed findings from the pipeline).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/orchestration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Initially should we try to use OpenAI Agents to try and build out the pipeline and then use Astra as the model for data analytics?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="280" width="400" x="-1330" y="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
